Z||000003||Oreif||12-01-2001||01:37 PM||||AT&T used Excite's network for their broadband network. When Excite shut down at 6am this morning, AT&T went with it.<BR>When I called them they said I'd be down from hours to 3 weeks!!! Since we have had problems before, I am cancelling them and have already joined Earthlink. It's at 56K so it's a lot slower. (That's how I'm posting now!)<P>Tom,<BR>I got the payment, Emblems will be in mail first thing Monday morning.<P>and if Joe happens to see this, your tail lights will be going out UPS on Monday.<P>I'll try to be on-line tonight.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||12-01-2001||04:23 PM||||For those of you who don't know.....<P>Anything with @home after it is part of the Excite@home network. ATT, Comcast, and others use that net for their cable customers. (Yes, it's also related to the Excite search/portal. I believe the portal was recently sold.)<P>You can find out what is going on with the Excite@home bankruptcy proceedings at <A HREF="http://www.news.com" TARGET=_blank>www.news.com</A> <BR>Click on "This weeks headlines" for the whole story.<P>From todays report...<P>Customers throughout the United States told CNET News.com on early Saturday morning they could not access Web sites and were experiencing slow or flaky connections from their normally swift cable modems. Numerous Excite@Home customers, including those in California, Washington, Illinois and Michigan, said that service was down entirely, forcing them to revert to relatively lethargic dial-up service to send e-mail or surf the Web. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||12-01-2001||04:25 PM||||AT&T is working on it... Trust me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I doubt it'll be down for 3 weeks...<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000006||Max The Chainsaw||12-01-2001||06:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>AT&T is working on it... Trust me   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I doubt it'll be down for 3 weeks...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm sure it won't be down that long, I'm using it now.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||ThatRickGuy||12-01-2001||10:27 PM||||AT&T isn't going under, it's just @Home, I'm on Charter @Home (the local cable con-artists) last I heard, AT&T is trying to do a complete buy out of @home to keep the service going. other groups are trying to do the same in their service areas, like Charter Pipeline here. anyways, hopefully they'll get it sorted out soon.<P>-Rick||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||12-01-2001||11:02 PM||||With all the problems I've had with them I have decided to drop them. I am already signed up with Earthlink, and in January I will be hooked up via DSL Earthlink. Not as fast as cable but more reliable and a whole lot cheaper.<BR>I received an automated call from them.(AT&T) They said my particular area would take 2 to 10 days. My wife sells a bunch of stuff on Ebay. Many items end tomorrow. Since our mail server is shut down we would lose almost $600 (total of current bids) + get negative feedback and possibly banned from Ebay for not having a valid Email.<P>I had AT&T cable for a little over 2 years, Fast=yes, more reliable=not really,<BR>customer service= very crappy.<P>Update:<BR>Per Yahoo news, AT&T was the only one they shut off.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  This is apparently because AT&T is being accused of steering Excite towards bankruptcy in order to buy them. It also says AT&T's present network structure can only hold 20% of the 850,000 customers affected!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> It even shows a 2-10 day period for Illinois.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||8
